# Runtime-uploaded user content (photos, attachments) lives under an app's
# public/ dir and gets synced live -> source/ like any other file, but it is
# user data, not app code, and must never reach this public repo.
# make-zip.sh ships the empty directory so installs still get the folder.
source/apps/*/public/*upload*/

# Premium add-on content lives in an app's premium/ dir. It is delivered from
# mvmos.org to subscribers only and must never reach this public repo or the
# public zip — make-zip.sh skips it for the same reason.
#
# The trailing slash is deliberate: these patterns match the *directory* only.
# apps/<id>/premium.json is a different thing — it is the public description of
# what a subscription adds, read from this repo by mvmos.org to build the app
# page and the premium page, and it must stay committed. Do not turn these into
# `source/apps/*/premium*` or the site loses every premium listing.
source/apps/*/premium/
source/backend/apps/*/premium/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
